 once  he arrived on the island  so that they can't communicate with each  other or with him pixis begins to grill  elena  as the entire time she's been on the  island she's tried to make herself  appear squeaky clean  pixis notes that many months ago before  erin infiltrated mali  elena had flock assigned to her as a  guard and now he's in jail for trying to  build up support for eren among the  population  remember how when elena first appeared  she commented how excited she was to  finally see erin  and then in one of the other flashbacks  she tried to properly meet him but levi  got in the way  whatever elena is thinking she's clearly  a big fan of eren and obviously a big  fan of zeke as well  so there's something going on and it's  just very unclear what  pixie states that the place elena was  staying was not that far away from  aaron's home  meaning it's possible that with the help  of flock aaron and elena had a secret  meeting  if flock thought it was beneficial for  aaron to meet elena then yeah of course  he would let that happen so i guess  we'll find out the truth next week  now back in the stables gabby and falca  were working as farmhands  and even this horse can tell that gabby  has bad vibes most of the scene was  pretty self-explanatory but we did get  this moment when gabby asked falco why  he's not more angry with zeke  and the true reason is that he's not  really reacting to zeke's betrayal  because falco himself feels incredibly  guilty for the part that he played  everything that transpired would not  have happened if falco didn't deliver  those letters for aaron  so he doesn't feel quite right in being  totally angry with zeke  when he himself is at fault after this  moment when they're taking a break  kaya makes it clear that she knew they  were from mali the entire time  but chose not to say anything because  unlike a certain someone  kaia doesn't judge a person based on  where they're from for the remainder of  the episode gabby's mali and  brainwashing was working at nearly a  hundred percent  as she kept trying to justify everything  bad that's happened to both kaya  and the other orphans who live on the  farm her logic was that because of the  atrocities committed by the eldians  present-day aliens deserve anything bad  that happens to them of course that  logic doesn't quite check out  but the thing that really amazed me was  that gabby was so  insensitive that she would even say  these things on the spot  where kai's mother was literally eaten  by a titan why does falco like this girl  again like  what redeeming quality does gaby have  that makes him so in love with her  when he's clearly the only sane one  among the two of them in fact a few  episodes ago  falco tried to tell gabi that the attack  on mali was because mali attacked  parodies first  and gabby replied saying something like  did you see it so  i guess this is her literally seeing it  like this is what marley did so in that  sense it's quite poetic that she's here  the post-credits scene for this episode  occurs in mali and just before you start  freaking out not every episode has a  post-credit scene so don't go back  looking at the previous episodes  only like i think this is only the  second one to have one maybe the third  but anyway anyway the malian warriors  finally realized that zeke has betrayed  them  and there were a few things that gave  him away for example there is mali and  technology integrated into the scouts  equipment  and because peak knows that elena was  sent to paris a few years ago  it's kind of obvious that zeke was the  one who organized everything magath also  elaborates that zeke's full remains were  not found  from the perspective of the malians they  thought that there would be more stuff  in the beast titan but really it was  just his limbs  all the warriors take the news  differently with poco being the most  emotional as usual  but colt who is meant to be the next  beast titan is also quite concerned but  you know not as much as you might expect  that's because colt's main priority is  getting falco back home  which can only be done once mali decide  to launch their counter attack on  parodies  magat's idea is to wait six months  before they attack the island which gets  a big reaction out of colt because you  know that's way too long  but magath's reasoning is pretty sound  mcgath wants to give other countries  around the world enough time to prepare  and by doing this they can all attack  the island simultaneously  if that was to happen parodies would not  stand a chance the only way they would  survive  is if they had already activated the  rumbling otherwise there's just nothing  that would save them  from the entire world attacking them at  once that said  reiner argues that instead of waiting  they should launch a surprise attack on  the island straight away  as by doing that zeke and the rest of  the people on the island would be in no  way prepared  no one on paradise is expecting mali to  attack so soon  especially after armin destroyed a chunk  of their army so by launching a quick  attack  they can stop whatever zeke is planning  to do with that said that was my  breakdown for episode 11 of attack on  titan season 4.  as usual i'd appreciate if you dropped a  like if you liked this one and let me  know in the comments what you thought of  the episode  until the next one peace out
 

